# SafeMining MCP and Console

## Project gate

At the start of any Unity work, call `Unity_ManageEditor` `GetProjectRoot`.

Abort if the root is not `D:/Unity/Projects/SafeMiningVR`. Do not call `ManageScene` Load/Save, `ManageGameObject`, or other write tools against a different project.

## Unity MCP

When Unity MCP is available:

- Author scenes and prefabs with `Unity_ManageScene` / `Unity_ManageGameObject`
- Do not hand-edit scene or prefab YAML
- After each block of work, call `Unity_ReadConsole` with Errors; require 0 entries
- Validate scripts with Unity MCP tools, not a second Editor batch compile while this project is already open

## Meta VR MCP

When a change touches Quest, XRI, teleport, grab, world-space HUD, comfort, or Android build: call `meta_docs_search` (and `meta_docs_get_page` if needed) before deciding. Keep XRI 3.3.1 unless docs require a specific API change.

## Console

- 0 Error type messages in compile, Play Mode, and menu to simulation flows
- `Debug.LogError` only for irrecoverable setup failure
- Pedagogical rejects use localized subtitles, not `LogError`
- Fix warnings introduced by our changes

## Assets

- SafeMining `.meta` GUIDs must be 32 hex characters
- Do not recreate a gameplay `asmdef` that cannot see `ControlCenter`
